{
  "date": "2026-10-14",
  "scope": "Analysis only. Existing six Nav2 trials plus six isolated fixed-command Isaac trials. No production code, runtime configuration, thresholds or USD edits.",
  "conclusion_ko": "6~7도는 실제 차체 과회전이며 최종 허용 2.865도를 넘는다. 저속 구동 응답 저하와 PI 보정 누적, 측정 속도를 따르는 RPP 감속 제한, 정지 확인 없는 Nav2 순간 도착 판정 뒤 제동 지연이 연결된다. 저속 구동 저항의 정확한 접촉/물성 원인은 아직 미확정이다.",
  "confirmed": [
    "Final arrival check waits for stopped odometry for 0.8 simulation seconds, then checks pose at that stamp. It correctly rejects >0.05rad yaw error.",
    "All six trials map/world stopped yaw differ by at most 0.184deg at nearest samples within 0.134 simulation seconds. Failed trials applied zero AprilTag corrections.",
    "At fixed cmd_w=-0.06, nominal wheel target magnitude is 0.156496rad/s. Before failures, simulator PI wheel targets reach 1.81/1.89/1.99rad/s while motion is initially small.",
    "RPP rotate_to_heading_angular_vel=0.06 is a desired value, not a hard cap. Installed Nav2 1.3.12 clamps desired angular command to measured odom_w plus/minus max_angular_accel/control_frequency (1.2/20=0.06), then applies an angle-based stopping cap. This permits approximately -0.30 commands when measured velocity is approximately -0.36.",
    "Selected SimpleGoalChecker checks position/yaw and ignores twist. Nav2 can succeed during passage through target heading, after which the separate final arrival check finds braking overshoot.",
    "Zero command resets PI integral and applies reverse braking targets. Overshoot is not caused by an integral that remains accumulated after stop.",
    "Fixed-command trials without ROS/Nav2 reproduced severe low-speed response loss at about -71deg both near the bed and at the station. Station initial -90deg responds much better. Each condition is a single trial, and spawning fresh is not an exact replay of arrival contact history.",
    "Removing PI also severely reduces rotation at the normal station pose on CPU and GPU; disabling PI is not a demonstrated fix."
  ],
